			)
		)
		(uuid "545e38f2-67cd-4929-af4a-a92ddd6016c4")
	)
	(text "This PCB controls the Azimuth and Elevation axes of a satellite dish.\nThis is a DIY project for now. The target application is amateur radio astonomy.\n\nThe initial dish for testing is a 3-meter satellite dish that needs precise \npointing of under 1 degree accuracy for high frequencies from 1.2GHz to 8.4GHz.\n\nThe PCB outputs PWM to control a stepper motor. Feedback is from an encoder on\nthe axis. The Raspberry Pi uses a PID loop to adjust the speed and position of\nthe motor.\n\nI2C sensors placed at each axis monitor temperature and humidity at the motors \nand gears."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 133.35 115.57 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 2.286 2.286)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "5f33f292-66e5-4900-b9ba-42ca8a13a86c")
	)
